# L §5.19: "A reading whose value is none states no balance: it neither pads nor anchors, and with replace it removes
# the reading it replaces, as replace bank[r18] = none removes a movement." The none reading of 2026-02-28 leaves
# konto at its opening, 1 000.00; the 1 500.00 reading of 2026-03-31 pads 500.00. s3 replaces the 2 000.00 reading of
# 2026-05-31 with none: q2 stays at 1 500.00; as known 2026-06-15, before s3, that reading pads 500.00 (q3).
# (Writer 6: was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §5.19; a replace of a balance reading by none was LOAD-REPLACE.)
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source bank "bank"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place unexplained: outside lives 1900-01-01..

version open
  cite bank
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"

version s1
  cite bank
  known 2026-04-01
  pad konto from unexplained
  stated[konto] = 1 500.00 PLN at 2026-03-31 end "saldo"
  stated[konto] = none at 2026-02-28 end "brak"

version s2
  cite bank
  known 2026-06-01
  pad konto from unexplained
  stated[konto] = 2 000.00 PLN at 2026-05-31 end "saldo"

version s3
  cite bank
  known 2026-07-01
  pad konto from unexplained
  replace stated[konto] = none at 2026-05-31 end "korekta"

ask q1: bal(konto, 2026-02-28), bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
ask q2: bal(konto, 2026-06-30)
ask q3: bal(konto, 2026-06-30) as known 2026-06-15
=== expect
q1: (1 000.00 PLN, 1 500.00 PLN)
  pad: konto 2026-03-31 end, pads:s1:konto@2026-03-31 end of 500.00 PLN
  cut 2026-10-20
q2: 1 500.00 PLN
  pad: konto 2026-03-31 end, pads:s1:konto@2026-03-31 end of 500.00 PLN
  cut 2026-10-20
q3: 2 000.00 PLN
  pad: konto 2026-05-31 end, pads:s2:konto@2026-05-31 end of 500.00 PLN
  cut 2026-06-15
